UPDC scientific publication citation policy
===========================================

UPDC is distributed under the MIT License in LICENSE.

For scholarly or other publication use, including journal papers, conference
proceedings, theses/dissertations, technical reports, data-release papers, or
other published work that uses the UPDC code, its algorithmic implementation,
or scientific results produced with UPDC, the UPDC project requires citation
of BOTH publications below:

1. Wang, L., Li, G., & Kang, X. 2022, "Towards super-resolution via iterative
   multi-exposure coaddition", Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical
   Society, 517, 787. doi:10.1093/mnras/stac2664

2. Wang, L., Shan, H., Nie, L., et al. 2025, "UPdec-Webb: A Data Set for
   Coaddition of JWST NIRCam Images", The Astrophysical Journal Supplement
   Series, 276, 36. doi:10.3847/1538-4365/ad9566

Machine-readable citation metadata and BibTeX entries are provided in
CITATION.cff and CITATION.md.

This publication-citation policy is a scientific attribution policy of the
UPDC project. It is separate from, and does not modify, the permissions and
conditions of the MIT License.
